{"overview":"Eve Mason, a white-passing black woman, moves to a remote cottage she inherited from her late father. She makes the acquaintance of her neighbor, a dashing black settler named Hugh Van Allen, and quickly falls for him. Trouble brews as the local cadre of racist hucksters want the valuable land Van Allen lives on, and will do anything to take it from him.","cast":[{"n":"Iris Hall","c":"Evon \"Eve\" Mason","p":"/4yqztPkuQVbke0R3OtJnm0zbhzv.jpg","q":"Q119217900"},{"n":"Walker Thompson","c":"Hugh Van Allen","p":"/qcMx22d2jdCVvjXUDFE16CRPIGY.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Lawrence Chenault","c":"Jefferson Driscoll","p":"/vcNaTOgR0HnhA4W3KbC1PjxvFwy.jpg","q":"Q6503918"},{"n":"Mattie Wilkes","c":"Mother Driscoll","p":"/6rnxvwoGlOsWesyLJNuyqRSQtq0.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Louis Dean","c":"August Barr","p":"/obs2rP3VSKKZTNxgPbGyHmrlZFy.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Leigh Whipper","c":"Tugi - an Indian Fakir","p":"/3aDpK0wYeYrjahs02WhBWWmU8fV.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Jim Burris","c":"","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"E.G. Tatum","c":"Abraham","p":"/9s6d6uF5XinsQSTbIgq2SDlPZJ8.jpg","q":null},{"n":"James Burrough","c":"","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"George Catlin","c":"Dick Mason","p":null,"q":null}],"country":["United States"],"language":["English"],"wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Symbol_of_the_Unconquered","qid":"Q7767805","rel":{"US":{"d":"1920-11-28"}},"backdrops":["/tSW7uUI9IF5hL6K8XrtydktFmtt.jpg"]}